module

-- The root of the `@MINI@` library: the same calculus as `@CALCULUS@`, cut down
-- to a handful of rules.
--
-- Its whole purpose is build time, and it is worth having only for a calculus
-- big enough to have a build-time problem. The full package takes minutes to
-- elaborate; this one takes seconds, so a proof about the checker itself -- an
-- invariant, a preservation lemma, the soundness argument -- can be developed
-- against it and moved over once it holds. It is compiled from the same
-- signature by `install/install-@CALCLOWER@.sh --mini`, with `--rules` naming
-- the subset and no parser, so it is not a different calculus.
--
-- No executable and no parser: nothing here reads a proof file.
public import @MINI@.@CHECKER@
import all @MINI@.@CHECKER@
public import @MINI@.SmtEval
import all @MINI@.SmtEval
public import @MINI@.SmtModel
import all @MINI@.SmtModel
public import @MINI@.Spec
import all @MINI@.Spec

-- The proofs under `@MINI@/Proofs/` are deliberately not imported here: build
-- them directly, which is the point of having this package at all.

public section
